gands in 1.5% agarose gel buffered with TBE buffer: (A,E)DHLA; (B) DHLA&#x02013;PEG600; (C)DHLA&#x02009;:&#x02009;DHLA&#x02013;TEG&#x02013;Biotin (7&#x02009;:&#x02009;1); (D)DHLA&#x02013;PEG600&#x02009;:&#x02009;DHLA&#x02013;TEG&#x02013;Biotin (7&#x02009;:&#x02009;1).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2007-90651.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Luminescence image set of 540 nm emittingCdSe&#x02013;ZnS QD with DHLA&#x02013;PEG600&#x02009;:&#x02009;DHLA&#x02013;TEG&#x02013;Biotin (4&#x02009;:&#x02009;1) atpH 5.5 &#x0223c; 9 in phosphate buffer saline at various pH values at roomtemperature. Samples were excited with ahandheld UV lamp at 365&#x02009;nm.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2007-90651.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Surface binding plate assay of QD's withdifferent surface ligands: (<bold>1</bold>) DHLA,(2) DHLA&#x02013;PEG600, (3)DHLA&#x02009;:&#x02009;DHLA&#x02013;TEG&#x02013;Biotin (at 4&#x02009;:&#x02009;1 ratio), and (4) DHLA&#x02013;PEG600&#x02009;:&#x02009;DHLA&#x02013;TEG&#x02013;Biotin (at 4&#x02009;:&#x02009;1ratio). 540&#x02009;nm emitting QD's were used.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JBB2007-90651.004"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>